  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Define the required result before writing logic: Stations execute in order and every actuator is off after a passing tote discharges.",
      "Treat inspection_ok as simulator-to-PLC inputs. The PLC should command only conveyor_run, fill_valve_open, capper_run, labeler_run, inspection_run.",
      "Use a step/state approach and prove the transition order: index to fill \u2192 fill \u2192 index to cap \u2192 cap \u2192 index to label \u2192 label \u2192 index to inspect \u2192 inspect \u2192 discharge \u2192 ready.",
      "The 3D Start button pulses the explicit BOOL ladder input binding operator.start while the controller is running. A compatible PLC program must implement the station sequence; this binding alone does not provide controller-driven tote travel or a validated finishing process.",
      "Under a controller clock, conveyor_run now moves the tote at a prescribed 0.75 m/s with supported exit retention. PC tote_position and station-window feedback are available to PLC logic. The PLC must sequence its own station stops and commands. Normalized fill is now modeled; cap/label application and inspection remain open, and litre/flow calibration is unverified.",
      "The finishing tote now uses an unapproved scene-specific hollow/open-port candidate. Its separate fill cap is initially hidden; cap application is not yet implemented. The generic closed IBC remains a separate catalog asset.",
      "Controller-clocked fill is an illustrative normalized quantity, 20 percent per second, bounded to 0\u2013100 percent. It requires a stationary tote at the fill station, an open cap and actual nozzle-to-bore eligibility. PC fill_percent, fill_complete, fill_inhibited and actual_fill_percent_per_second report this model; litres and flow calibration remain unverified. Stop retains fill; Reset empties it.",
      "The candidate cap now has an open underside and seats at the neck rim. It remains initially hidden; cap application is not yet connected. The finishing installation uses a prescribed 140 mm nozzle stroke to retain bore engagement with this candidate scale."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is one valid functional reference. The same behavior may be implemented in LAD, FBD, or SCL; the rung layout is not prescribed.",
      "steps": [
        "index to fill: conveyor_run = true.",
        "fill: conveyor_run = false, fill_valve_open = true.",
        "index to cap: fill_valve_open = false, conveyor_run = true.",
        "cap: conveyor_run = false, capper_run = true.",
        "index to label: capper_run = false, conveyor_run = true.",
        "label: conveyor_run = false, labeler_run = true.",
        "index to inspect: labeler_run = false, conveyor_run = true.",
        "inspect: conveyor_run = false, inspection_run = true.",
        "discharge: inspection_run = false, conveyor_run = true.",
        "ready: conveyor_run = false."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Stations execute in order and every actuator is off after a passing tote discharges."
    },
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "A small chemical tote is filled, capped, labeled, inspected, and discharged through a five-station finishing line.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state.",
        "The PLC is ready to command conveyor_run, fill_valve_open, capper_run, labeler_run, inspection_run."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "index to fill",
        "fill",
        "index to cap",
        "cap",
        "index to label",
        "label",
        "index to inspect",
        "inspect",
        "discharge",
        "ready"
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "A normal stop removes PLC-owned commands and leaves the equipment in a safe state.",
        "Reset returns the scene to its documented initial condition."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing, stale, or incorrectly typed input must not be replaced by simulator logic.",
        "A missing PLC command leaves the affected equipment stopped and the test diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "Stations execute in order and every actuator is off after a passing tote discharges."
      ]
    },
